rg: GXEMUL-SEC/src/include/*: IO error for operation on GXEMUL-SEC/src/include/*: The filename, directory name, or volume label syntax is incorrect. (os error 123)

codex
The source checks show problems in (G) as written: its cascade update can leave pending interrupts without a CPU assertion, and the shared EOI change would give unconverted IACK users the same incomplete behavior that D1 rejects. I’m checking the proposed test rows against those gaps before assigning dispositions.


exec
"C:\\WINDOWS\\System32\\WindowsPowerShell\\v1.0\\powershell.exe" -Command "rg -n 'last_int|pending_timer_interrupts|pic[12]->isr|pic[12]->irr|bus_isa_init' GXEMUL-SEC/src; rg -n -C 5 'INTERRUPT_ASSERT|INTERRUPT_DEASSERT' GXEMUL-SEC/src/include/interrupt.h; rg -n -C 4 'DEV_GT_LENGTH|GT_PCI0_INTR_ACK' GXEMUL-SEC/src/include" in C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL
exec
