GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/i8259eoiirr/pass1_20261025/codex_t19p1.txt:93:| **B** | Adds service state, but does not cure the PIT: EOI clears ISR and immediately makes the still-pending request eligible again. Poll-only acknowledgement also leaves other vector paths untreated. |
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/i8259eoiirr/pass1_20261025/codex_t19p1.txt:94:| **C** | Can preserve the current distinction between repeatedly delivered timer events and held device requests, but needs an explicit producer/mode contract. Keeping PIT IRR clearing does not itself retire its pending-event count. It is not a complete edge model merely because a device never deasserts. |
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/i8259eoiirr/pass1_20261025/codex_t19p1.txt-95-| **D** | Restoring a bit from an independently maintained high level has A’s held-level effect. The PIT would also remain high. Shadow ownership must include V3 and cascade behavior; Jazz’s destructively cleared latch is not an independent physical-level shadow. |
