GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/i8259eoiirr/pass1_20261025/codex_t19p1.txt-116-
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/i8259eoiirr/pass1_20261025/codex_t19p1.txt-117-**READ:** `dev_prep.c`, `DEVICE_ACCESS(prep)`, and `dev_gt.c`, `GT_PCI0_INTR_ACK`, return `last_int` without setting ISR. Footbridge’s corresponding vector read likewise does not establish PIC service state. Jazz uses a separate controller, so it should not be described as another consumer of this PIC’s ISR.
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/i8259eoiirr/pass1_20261025/codex_t19p1.txt-118-
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/i8259eoiirr/pass1_20261025/codex_t19p1.txt-119-**DERIVED:** Accepting the supplied Linux flow, A preserves an asserted request through EOI. It becomes deliverable whenever masking permits—normally at unmask after handling. For a source that remains asserted, renewed delivery is consistent with level behavior. With the current PIT, however, there is no normal completion that removes the pending assertion. B merely suppresses it while ISR remains set and releases it again at EOI.
