GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/i8259eoiirr/pass1_20261025/grok_t19p1.txt:1:I will audit the premises against `GXEMUL-SEC/src/` before judging the design. First I am checking that this tree is the fork, then I will enumerate every writer of the PIC request and in-service bits.The `src/` writers of `irr` are a short list. I am reading those functions and the 8253 and OCW2 encodings next, so the design is judged from the producers rather than from the brief's summary.**NOT READY.** Do not ship (A) as written. The End-Of-Interrupt (EOI) edit in (A) is the datasheet-correct half, and the witness fix column matches it for an EOI that was not preceded by an acknowledge. Shipping that edit alone removes the only request-consume this model has. NetBSD/malta polls and then specific-EOIs inside one loop, Linux/malta acknowledges through the Galileo GT IACK register (which does not acknowledge), and the 8253 never deasserts. None of (B), (C), (D), or (E) is shippable unchanged. (C) is the closest supplied split, and the clear it depends on executes in `DEVICE_ACCESS(8259)`, not in the ISA layer.
